  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The New Utopia Begins Here: Hermina Huiswoud, 2019



    IRIS KENSMIL



    In
    her portraits, Kensmil focuses on black people who played important roles in
    history. Hermina Huiswoud (1905-1998) was a political activist. She belonged
    to a generation of anti-colonial thinkers, leaders and organizers who were active
    in the fight against European and American imperialism. After the Second World
    War she worked in Amsterdam, and as a supporter of the Our Suriname Association
    (VOS) fought for the independence of the Dutch colony. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
