  m_text: Rembrandt's pupils also painted realistically. This painting by Govert
    Flinck from 1640 may have been modeled on a black man who lived nearby. Flinck
    carefully studied the man's facial expression and gestures in order to paint
    a fantasy figure that he could sell on the market.
