  m_text: "Few portraits of black people were made in the seventeenth century. That
    is to say images of a particular person where the recognizability of that individual
    is concerned. However, there are portraits of black people, but mostly as servants
    of the white elite. Unfortunately we seldom know the sitter\u2019s identity. "
